From 470cdf1729d79627d198f27e4743be7b270700e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jordan Williams Johnson <jordandwj@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 03:25:23 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 11/12] etnaviv/ml: Keep graph outputs in cached memory

The CPU reads every graph output back, and reading the write-combined
tensor buffers is slow even with one bulk copy. Mark graph outputs, and
the buffers they alias through a bypass or a split, as read by the CPU,
and let etna_buffer_bo_new() allocate such buffers cached on arm64, as
etnaviv already does for textures with ETNA_RESOURCE_FLAG_CPU_READ.
The kernel invalidates them at CPU_PREP and cleans them at CPU_FINI.
The zero fill at creation now happens between a prep and a fini, so no
dirty cache line can later overwrite what the NPU writes.

On a VIPNano-QI.7120 (A311D), reading back a 786 KB int8 output went
from 2.6 ms to 1.5 ms; small outputs are unchanged. Alternating two
inputs over 2800 checked invokes gave no stale output.

Generated-by: LLM
